f-full kettle.","Pour it into a saucepan with 1/4 tsp salt on high heat.","Boil the rice, 12-13 mins.","Once cooked, drain, pop back in the pan and cover.","Meanwhile, chop the pepper into 2cm chunks."],"notes":[],"image":"/data/food/photos/steps/6630fd8efe45b17bd5360d1d-1.jpg","title":"Boil Rice"},{"points":["Heat a drizzle of oil in a frying pan on high heat.","Once hot, fry the pork mince, pepper, sugar snap peas and Thai style spice mix (add less if you'd prefer things milder), 5-6 mins.","Break up the pork as it cooks, then drain the fat.","Season with salt and pepper."],"notes":[{"kind":"important","text":"Wash hands and utensils after handling raw meat. Cook so there's no pink in the middle."}],"image":"/data/food/photos/steps/6630fd8efe45b17bd5360d1d-2.jpg","title":"Get Frying"},{"points":["Stir in the ketjap manis, rice vinegar, soy, sugar, ketchup (see pantry for both) and a splash of water.","Simmer, 1 min. Remove from the heat.","Taste and season with salt and pepper if needed."],"notes":[],"image":"/data/food/photos/steps/6630fd8efe45b17bd5360d1d-3.jpg","title":"Sauce Time"},{"points":["Share the rice between your bowls.","Spoon over the sweet and sticky pork.","Sprinkle over the sesame seeds."],"notes":[],"image":"/data/food/photos/steps/6630fd8efe45b17bd5360d1d-4.jpg","title":"Dinner's Ready!"}]}